			"notes": {
				"rationale": "bitte um Verzeihung is the Locution VERB um Verzeihung bitten, not a routine formula: it conjugates freely (sie bat um Verzeihung), and Duden (jemanden um Verzeihung bitten) and OpenThesaurus list it as a verb phrase, so ich is a unit of its own (user ruling R6, 2026-10-03). um and Verzeihung are fixed members (de/fixed-member-test). It apologizes, so it takes the 🙇 of Entschuldigung. für die Wartezeit is free: für names the reason, as wegen could (Duden Entschuldigung: jemanden für etwas, wegen etwas um Entschuldigung bitten), and no word of the expression governs it. Duden codes no für for Verzeihung, nor does verzeihen (jemandem etwas verzeihen), and bitten takes für only for Fürsprache (Duden bitten 2). So für is an adjunct's preposition, unlike the für of vielen Dank (de/governed-preposition-joins-its-governor, ADR 0034; decided by an agent under the user's delegation, 2026-10-02, #853). Knowledge (#884): Nom S · (Acc S), since ich bitte um Verzeihung is complete without jemanden, as bitten (Acc) (um + Acc); no Locution Type, because bitten keeps its own meaning 'ask for' and the forgiver is not the subject, so it is no Funktionsverbgefüge; synonyms sich entschuldigen, um Entschuldigung bitten and um Vergebung bitten from the OpenThesaurus synset. Decided by agents under the user's delegation. The Apology Formula Role is lost: only an INTJ carries one.",
				"knownMistakes": [
					"Taking für into the expression: it marks the reason, as wegen could, and no word of the expression governs it.",
					"Taking ich into the expression as an INTJ formula: um Verzeihung bitten conjugates freely."
				]
			},
